# Scheduled Tasks

This directory contains templates for running sync and reflection on a schedule.

## macOS (launchd)

| File | Schedule | What it runs | Secrets |
|------|----------|--------------|---------|
| `com.claude.daily-sync.plist` | Daily at 20:00 | `data-sync` skill | {% if sync_needs_secrets %}yes: wrapped in `op run` (Todoist token){% else %}none: plain `uv run`{% endif %} |
{%- if schedule_reflection %}
| `com.claude.weekly-reflect.plist` | Sunday at 09:00 | `weekly-reflection` skill | yes: `op run` (LLM API key) |
{%- endif %}
{%- if reflection_reminder %}
| `com.claude.reflection-reminder.plist` | Sunday at 10:00 | `scripts/reflection-reminder.sh` | none |
{%- endif %}

{% if sync_needs_secrets -%}
The daily sync needs the Todoist token, so it runs through `op run`. Scheduled runs
need unattended 1Password authentication; interactive unlock prompts fail under launchd.
{%- else -%}
The daily sync needs no secrets (mbsync uses the Keychain, Microsoft To-Do uses the
msal token cache), so it runs `uv run` directly: no `op run`, no `.env`, no unlock prompt.
{%- endif %}
{%- if not schedule_reflection %}

The weekly reflection is **attended**: run it yourself (it calls an LLM via `op run`).
{%- if reflection_reminder %} The reminder notifies you on Sunday if no
`*-weekly-reflection.md` in `{{ reflections_dir }}` is newer than 6 days, and stays
silent otherwise.{% endif %} To schedule it instead, re-run `copier update` with
`schedule_reflection=true`.
{%- endif %}

The plists use Homebrew paths for `uv`{% if sync_needs_secrets or schedule_reflection %} and `op`{% endif %}; adjust them to your installation.

### Install

```bash
mkdir -p {{ launchd_logs | quote }}
# Only the jobs enabled for this vault (`copier update` never deletes a plist that is
# no longer generated, so a stale one may still sit in config/).
for job in daily-sync{% if schedule_reflection %} weekly-reflect{% endif %}{% if reflection_reminder %} reflection-reminder{% endif %}; do
  cp "config/com.claude.$job.plist" ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
  launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.claude.$job.plist
done
launchctl list | grep com.claude
```
{%- if not schedule_reflection %}

If an older version installed `com.claude.weekly-reflect`, the uninstall loop below removes it;
delete `config/com.claude.weekly-reflect.plist` too.
{%- endif %}

Run a job once now: `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.claude.daily-sync`.

### Logs

All launchd logs go to `{{ launchd_logs }}/` (`sync-*.log`{% if schedule_reflection %}, `reflect-*.log`{% endif %}{% if reflection_reminder %}, `reflection-reminder-*.log`{% endif %}).

### Uninstall

```bash
for p in ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.claude.*.plist; do
  launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u) "$p" && rm "$p"
done
```

### Prerequisite: Full Disk Access

On recent macOS, the launchd-spawned process needs Full Disk Access to read email, browser, and other sources. Grant it to:

- `/opt/homebrew/bin/uv`{% if sync_needs_secrets or schedule_reflection %} and `/opt/homebrew/bin/op`{% endif %} (the binaries invoked by the plists)
- Or Terminal.app if you prefer to run manually

System Settings → Privacy & Security → Full Disk Access.

### Customizing the schedule

Edit the `StartCalendarInterval` dict. `Weekday` uses `0 = Sunday`, `1 = Monday`, etc.

```xml
<key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
<dict>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>7</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer>
</dict>
```

For multiple run times, make `StartCalendarInterval` an array of dicts.

## Linux (cron)

Use `crontab.example` instead (`crontab -e`, then paste its lines).

## Manual Runs

Any time, from `{{ logic }}`:

```bash
{% if sync_needs_secrets %}op run --env-file=.env -- {% endif %}uv run .claude/skills/data-sync/sync_all.py --yes
op run --env-file=.env -- uv run --project .claude/skills/weekly-reflection .claude/skills/weekly-reflection/weekly_reflection.py
```
